WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.835
-President Trump is retaliating

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:05.104
against impeachment witnesses
as his attorney general

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:06.739
works with his personal lawyer

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:09.275
to continue to digging up dirt
on his political rivals.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.210
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:15.748
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:18.851
There's one very specific thing
Donald Trump loves doing,

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:21.220
and that's showing off
pieces of paper.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.223
He's done it multiple times with
letters from world leaders,

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:27.326
supposedly secret deals with
other countries,

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:29.428
and just last week, he did it
again when he held up

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:31.564
newspaper headlines showing off
his acquittal

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.033
at two separate events,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.934
including
the National Prayer Breakfast

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.703
and a White House press
conference.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.471
I think I know what's
going on here.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:41.006
Trump's desperate to prove
to us that he knows how to read,

00:00:41.006 --> 00:00:42.541
except no one's buying it.

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:45.344
I mean, when your dog carries
the paper into the house,

00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:46.613
no one thinks, "Wow,

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:49.148
he must be really up to date
on current events."

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:50.616
"Hey, Rusty, are you happy
with the way

00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:52.284
the Democratic Party
handled Iowa?"

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.287
[ Growling ]
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.388
Trump's like an idiot frat bro
trying to impress girls

00:00:56.388 --> 00:00:59.258
by wearing glasses and carrying
around a book of poetry.

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:01.961
"Oh, this?
This is just my favorite poet,

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.762
Ralph Waldo Emerson.

00:01:03.762 --> 00:01:05.732
You know, he was famously
very hard to find.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.367
They wrote a book about it.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.369
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:10.703
[ Applause ]

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.539
But there he is.
There he is."

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:16.475
Well, Trump did it again on
Friday when he greeted the press

00:01:16.475 --> 00:01:18.778
at his daily chopper-adjacent
Q-and-yell

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.346
on the White House lawn.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:23.015
Trump was holding up an appeals
court decision dismissing

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:26.352
a lawsuit by Democrats, claiming
Trump's business conflicts

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.054
violate a part
of the Constitution

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.255
called the Emoluments Clause.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.257
Now this is only one of three
such lawsuits,

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:33.492
and it was only dismissed
because the court found

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:36.128
that individual lawmakers
can't sue the president

00:01:36.128 --> 00:01:37.897
on behalf of the entire
Congress.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.199
But clearly Trump hadn't
read the actual decision.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:42.669
In fact, he admitted he hadn't
read it.

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:45.504
-So I just got this.
It was just handed to me.

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:48.074
This is the D.C. Circuit.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:51.344
And we just won the big
emoluments case.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:54.013
I think it was a unanimous
decision.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:57.717
This was brought by Nancy Pelosi
and her group.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.519
Just came out a few minutes ago.

00:02:00.519 --> 00:02:02.955
So I'll be reading it
on the helicopter.

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.191
-No, you won't.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.493
There's no way you're getting
on to a helicopter

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.595
and reading a dense legal
document about something

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.564
called the Emoluments Clause.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.666
After you buckle in,
they probably hand you

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.202
a plastic control stick so you
can pretend you're the pilot.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.838
[ Laughter ]
"Ready for takeoff."

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.673
[ Applause ]

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:24.210
Still, that decision was Trump's

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.678
second legal victory
of the week.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.213
Last week, of course,
he was acquitted

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.315
by a Republican Senate
that locked arms

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.284
to protect him at any and all
costs,

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:33.652
